{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02YT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$G \\to F$", "MATH_0002": "$F' \\subset F$", "MATH_0003": "$G$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-immersions-monomorphisms}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-representable-transformations-property-implication}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-section-immersions}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:080dd6f1faa080d53eb236c9a89f4ca3a015df18c562a79f36d54aab06ad62e1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3a1f00caff5ea36029d24109dc424eac241629eeeda590d17d3844388de2a248", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe note that these definitions make sense since an immersion\nis in particular a monomorphism (see\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>\nand Lemma <REF_0002>),\nand hence the image of an\nimmersion <MATH_0001> of algebraic spaces is a subfunctor <MATH_0002>\nwhich is (canonically) isomorphic to <MATH_0003>. Thus some of the discussion\nof Schemes, Section <REF_0003> carries over to the\nsetting of algebraic spaces.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:98a387268f4aa01a2b46af07920ff3231af10910f17259473727a15fee7d5c47", "unit_id": "tag:02YT:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02YT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S \\in \\Ob(\\Sch_{fppf})$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-composition-immersions}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:75e0bd2a0154ce6e65bd6cb429246b47726475dbd7595f3cce635af1c9c30772", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:174cfbb8d44112c13c21d8b58e328599c33d26178de706e2bbc3f622ad8fec45", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nA composition of (closed, resp.<SPACE_0001>open) immersions of\nalgebraic spaces over <MATH_0002> is a (closed, resp.<SPACE_0002>open)\nimmersion of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6b52fa9e97405ac7ec04691f62cb88addc4b566551b263ae573585316cb99577", "unit_id": "tag:02YV:statement"}
