{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02YT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S \\in \\Ob(\\Sch_{fppf})$", "MATH_0002": "$F$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$F_1$", "MATH_0005": "$F_2$", "MATH_0006": "$F$", "MATH_0007": "$F_1 \\subset F_2$", "MATH_0008": "$F$", "MATH_0009": "$F_1$", "MATH_0010": "$F_2$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-sub-subspaces}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7a6682934703249cddf342f2cfa170d4b276ce5e5602adb6367eb8d2b0366e6a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cdab6f8b9fa71254b91e71f4e7c8b7a7632d1c1503751db9f2efae8a062a5cae", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>. Let <MATH_0004>, <MATH_0005> be\nlocally closed subspaces of <MATH_0006>. If <MATH_0007> as subfunctors\nof <MATH_0008>, then <MATH_0009> is a locally closed subspace of <MATH_0010>.\nSimilarly for closed and open subspaces.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:947a320255fcbb9b51a549311a402a0288dfe949e72163f5e4f8ef173f062300", "unit_id": "tag:02YX:statement"}
